  "description": "Roll out on dirt You get a hardtail mountain bike built for rough paths, gravel cuts, and daily rides that turn spiky fast. The front fork takes the edge off chatter, while the rigid rear keeps the frame direct and easy to read when you're picking a line. Feel the frame response Its frame has a clean, no-fuss finish and a shape that leaves room to move when the trail changes under you. Pedal hard. The bike stays quick under you, with the kind of simple setup that's easy to live with after a muddy loop or a stop at the bike rack. Reach for longer rides When you want one bike for fire roads, park paths, and weekend singletrack, this one fits that job. The controls stay plain and familiar, so you can focus on the climb, the descent, and the next corner instead of fiddling with the ride.",
